From f0149e0000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH 0149e] evergo: put the full panic text into the SWEETLOG ring

0148e mirrored sweet_early_putc() into SWEETLOG, but the early console is
disabled right after bootstrap ("SWEET EARLY 20: kprintf startup complete"),
so it only captured the 20 early markers. panic_trap_to_debugger() still
calls sweet_early_panic(), which returns immediately when early_disabled is
set - so the actual panic text never reaches SWEETLOG. That is why
read_sweetlog.py kept showing only the first ~1 s of each boot while the
screen showed a real panic.

Hook the correct layer: in panic_trap_to_debugger(), format the panic string
with vsnprintf() into a local buffer and feed it to sweet_log_append() BEFORE
any of the debugger/console paths run. sweet_log_append() is a lock-free
atomic write into a static ring (bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c), safe in panic context.
Prefix with "SWEET PANIC " so it is easy to find in the decoded ring.

This is observation-only: nothing about panic() behaviour changes.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/kern/debug.c b/osfmk/kern/debug.c
index 32694b1..ea67de1 100644
--- a/osfmk/kern/debug.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/debug.c
@@ -1199,6 +1199,30 @@ panic_trap_to_debugger(const char *panic_format_str, va_list *panic_args, unsign
 	evergo_anom_dump();
 	/* No CPU/thread/debugger state is required for this first panic copy. */
 	sweet_early_panic(panic_format_str, panic_args);
+	/*
+	 * evergo (0149e): the early console is disabled after bootstrap, so
+	 * sweet_early_panic() above returns immediately for any real panic and
+	 * its text is lost to SWEETLOG.  Format it here - before the debugger
+	 * path - and append it to the lock-free console ring so
+	 * read_sweetlog.py can finally show the full panic.
+	 */
+	{
+		extern void sweet_log_append(const char *c, int size);
+		char panic_log[1024];
+		va_list log_args;
+		va_copy(log_args, *panic_args);
+		int n = vsnprintf(panic_log, sizeof(panic_log),
+		    panic_format_str, log_args);
+		va_end(log_args);
+		if (n > 0) {
+			if (n >= (int)sizeof(panic_log)) {
+				n = (int)sizeof(panic_log) - 1;
+			}
+			sweet_log_append("SWEET PANIC ", 12);
+			sweet_log_append(panic_log, n);
+			sweet_log_append("\n", 1);
+		}
+	}
 #endif
 
 #if defined(__x86_64__) && (DEVELOPMENT || DEBUG)
